# Project Overview — Heroes on the Water

WordPress theme at `wp-content/themes/custom-theme`. Section-based, static-first architecture.

## Naming (mandatory)

| Item | Value |
|------|-------|
| Theme name | Heroes on the Water |
| PHP prefix | `hotw_*` |
| Constant | `HOTW_THEME_VER` |
| Text domain | `heros-on-the-water` |
| Package | `Heros_On_The_Water` |
| CSS prefix | `.hotw-*` |
| CSS variables | `--hotw-*` |
| Body classes | `hotw-home`, `hotw-whats-on` |

## Architecture

```
functions.php → inc/post-type-event.php, inc/whats-on-events.php
header.php / footer.php → page-template/header.php, page-template/footer.php
Page templates → get_template_part('template-parts/...') or require (What's On only)
```

## Key paths

- `template-parts/home/` — home sections (hero, purpose, wood, vibe, faq, cta, gallery)
- `template-parts/story/` — pizza slider, events-live, extras-live
- `template-parts/menu/` — classic, signature
- `template-parts/whats-on/` — calendar, upcoming (loaded via `require`)
- `assets/css/` — variables → common → style + responsive
- `assets/js/main.js` — mobile nav, Swiper, What's On tabs

## Do not introduce

- New architecture patterns unless explicitly requested
- Inline styles in PHP templates
- New `@media` blocks in `common.css`
- jQuery or build tooling without approval
